# yt-dlp config - managed by the bootstrap on every platform.
#
# Deployed to ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/yt-dlp/config on Linux and macOS
# and %APPDATA%\yt-dlp\config on Windows, the paths yt-dlp recommends. The
# whole file is the repo's; the first replacement is kept as config.bak.
# --ignore-config skips it for one download.
#
# The file name stays yt-dlp's default, "<title> [<id>].<ext>".

# Into ~/Downloads (%USERPROFILE%\Downloads on Windows) wherever you run it
# from. -P . for the current directory.
-P ~/Downloads

# Title, uploader, date and description in the file's tags, and chapters as
# real chapter marks.
--embed-metadata

# The thumbnail as cover art, and subtitles as tracks, rather than loose
# .webp and .vtt files beside the video. English and Ukrainian when the
# uploader provided them; auto-generated captions stay off.
--embed-thumbnail
--embed-subs
--sub-langs en.*,uk.*

# Matroska takes all of the above for any codec. YouTube's best video and
# audio merge into .webm by default, and yt-dlp cannot put a thumbnail in a
# .webm - the download would end in a post-processing error. mpv and VLC, both
# in the apps group, play .mkv.
--merge-output-format mkv
